From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:34:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] egl: create an image over memory the caller owns

The Apple GPU host runs vrend on Mesa's Zink driver, where the only way to
alias memory the caller already owns is GL_AMD_pinned_memory, which aliases it
as a buffer. A virtio-gpu host has to sample a guest's shared-memory scanout as
a 2D texture, so today it copies the pages into a texture on every read.

Zink can already build the image: it creates a VkImage with
VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo(HOST_ALLOCATION) and imports the pages with
VkImportMemoryHostPointerInfoEXT whenever VK_EXT_external_memory_host is
present, which is how pipe_screen::resource_from_user_memory is implemented.
What is missing is a GL-visible way to reach it for anything but a buffer.

EGL_MESA_image_host_pointer adds that: eglCreateImageKHR with the new
EGL_HOST_POINTER_MESA target takes the pointer as the client buffer plus
EGL_WIDTH, EGL_HEIGHT, EGL_LINUX_DRM_FOURCC_EXT, EGL_HOST_POINTER_PITCH_MESA,
EGL_HOST_POINTER_SIZE_MESA and an optional EGL_HOST_POINTER_OFFSET_MESA, and
the resulting image is used through GL_OES_EGL_image like any other. Only the
producer is new; the consumer half already exists.

The size is how many bytes the caller owns at the pointer, and it is
required. The driver imports whole rows from the pointer plus the offset, so
an image whose rows would reach past those bytes is refused: otherwise a
caller whose width, height, pitch or offset comes from someone it does not
trust would hand the driver memory it does not own.

Because the caller keeps the storage, the import must be all or nothing: the
resource is created with PIPE_BIND_LINEAR, and the stride the driver then
reports through PIPE_RESOURCE_PARAM_STRIDE has to equal the caller's pitch.
A format, alignment, size or pitch the driver cannot alias returns
EGL_NO_IMAGE_KHR instead of quietly copying, so the caller can choose its own
fallback once per resource rather than paying an unannounced copy per frame -
the reason a GL_APPLE_client_storage-shaped entry point was not used, since
that one is specified to be free to copy and offers no way to ask whether it
did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
